{
  "$schema": "./schema/flight_phase.schema.json",
  "design_notes": [
    "Table 9.1, one entry per row, in flight order. The field phase holds a flight-phase ID (F0 to F14, F7b); the field facts holds fact-bank IDs (F01 to F40). The two kinds share the letter F and never share a field.",
    "pilot_actions_key, console_duties_key and fact_moment_key are the cells as printed. console_roles lists the roles a cell names; all_consoles marks \"All consoles monitor\" and \"Everyone\".",
    "minigames is the Minigames column plus the minigames whose When line in 10.5 names the phase, so that this file and data/minigames.json agree; each difference from the column is noted on the phase. Conditions (\"if reusable fairing\", \"if engine-out\", \"at end\") are the triggers in data/minigames.json.",
    "possible_events splits the Possible events column into one entry per event. failure_mode links an event to the failure model of 8.4 where a row matches by name; the link is a reading, the table does not state it.",
    "facts links a fact moment to the fact bank only where the bank holds the same fact (F03 staging, F04 Max Q, F05 orbital speed, F17 entry corridor, F18 Orion parachutes, F19 blackout). The bank itself names a flight phase only for F05. The other fact moments (F0, F1, F2, F3, F6, F7b, F9, F13) have no bank entry and no source yet.",
    "The design does not group the phases into the flight segments used for pilot rotation (9.4) and assist levels (9.3: ascent, orbit, entry), so no segment is stored."
  ],
